WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.367 --> 00:00:02.936
SPEAKER:<i> Gary was a crop duster.</i>

00:00:03.002 --> 00:00:04.771
(AIRPLANES WHOOSHING)

00:00:04.838 --> 00:00:07.774
SPEAKER 2:<i> And the best pilot
 the TOPGUN program
 had ever known.</i>

00:00:07.841 --> 00:00:08.874
That's my dad.

00:00:09.909 --> 00:00:12.578
SPEAKER:<i> He walked away
 from 11 plane crashes.</i>

00:00:12.611 --> 00:00:14.747
SPEAKER 3:
<i> A special kind of wild man.</i>

00:00:14.781 --> 00:00:16.282
(AIRPLANE WHOOSHES)

00:00:16.916 --> 00:00:19.018
SPEAKER:<i> One morning,
when I'm driving to the country,</i>

00:00:19.052 --> 00:00:20.853
<i> the car had broken down,</i>

00:00:20.887 --> 00:00:22.255
<i> and all of a sudden...</i>

00:00:26.592 --> 00:00:28.761
<i> Gary jumped off the bridge.</i>

00:00:28.794 --> 00:00:29.762
(LIGHTNING CRACKS)

00:00:29.795 --> 00:00:31.097
SPEAKER 4:
<i> What made him do that?</i>

00:00:31.130 --> 00:00:32.432
(LIGHTNING CRACKS)

00:00:32.465 --> 00:00:34.367
SPEAKER 5:
<i> People had, like, theories.</i>

00:00:34.400 --> 00:00:35.301
(LIGHTNING CRACKS)

00:00:35.468 --> 00:00:37.036
SPEAKER 6:
<i> I know it was a shock...</i>

00:00:37.069 --> 00:00:38.304
(LIGHTNING CRACKS)

00:00:38.604 --> 00:00:40.640
SPEAKER 6:<i> ...but maybe
 it wasn't inexplicable.</i>

00:00:41.941 --> 00:00:45.712
I didn't think they talked
about our double life.

00:00:45.745 --> 00:00:48.615
♪ (DRAMATIC MUSIC PLAYS) ♪

00:00:48.648 --> 00:00:50.717
SPEAKER 7:<i> Gary became
an international drug smuggler,</i>

00:00:51.251 --> 00:00:53.553
and he had made millions
and millions of dollars.

00:00:54.087 --> 00:00:55.655
SPEAKER:<i> It gets complicated.</i>

00:00:55.721 --> 00:00:57.556
Your mind has to switch gears.

00:00:57.790 --> 00:01:00.560
<i>But I never once told the kids.</i>

00:01:00.593 --> 00:01:02.662
His wife ought to have
an Academy Award.

00:01:02.962 --> 00:01:04.797
♪ (MUSIC CONTINUES) ♪

00:01:04.830 --> 00:01:07.167
The war on drugs intensified
during that time.

00:01:08.734 --> 00:01:10.937
In the end, this was almost like
the tip of the iceberg.

00:01:12.171 --> 00:01:15.107
SPEAKER 8:<i> Gary was flying
 guns connected to the CIA.</i>

00:01:15.141 --> 00:01:17.343 line:0%
(ON RECORDING)

00:01:18.244 --> 00:01:20.313
♪ (MUSIC CONTINUES) ♪

00:01:20.346 --> 00:01:21.981
SPEAKER 9:
<i> My expectations were so high
 of my dad</i>

00:01:22.949 --> 00:01:23.983
that it broke me.

00:01:24.483 --> 00:01:25.952
SPEAKER 10:<i> You're part
 of what she experienced.</i>

00:01:27.086 --> 00:01:28.521
SPEAKER 11:<i> When you're dealing
 with that kind of money,</i>

00:01:28.587 --> 00:01:29.589
people act different.

00:01:30.189 --> 00:01:32.091
SPEAKER 12:<i> I don't think
 Gary Betzner had a clue</i>

00:01:32.125 --> 00:01:33.359
<i>of what he was tripping into...</i>

00:01:33.426 --> 00:01:36.162
♪ (MUSIC BUILDS) ♪

00:01:36.195 --> 00:01:38.197
SPEAKER 12:<i> ...one of
 the biggest political scandals</i>

00:01:38.264 --> 00:01:39.431
<i> of his lifetime.</i>

00:01:39.465 --> 00:01:44.504 line:0%
♪ (MUSIC PLAYS, FADES) ♪

